    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS, with the full acceptance suite (30 tests including Cp19) green and no regressions.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit rejecting with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100+ owners have been created for a given day (by `registrationDate`), following the codebase's existing exception-based pattern (mirroring `CityCapacityException`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`rest/advice/DailyOwnerLimitException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` thrown when the daily cap is hit.\n\n2. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DailyOwnerLimitException` that returns `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429) as a `ProblemDetail`, consistent with the other handlers.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after the registration date is defaulted to today (and before persisting), it now counts existing owners registered on that date; if the count is `>= 100` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`), it throws `DailyOwnerLimitException`. Added the `countOwnersRegisteredOn(LocalDate)` helper following the style of the existing `countOwnersInCity`/`countNamesakes` helpers.\n\nThe pinned acceptance test `Cp19Tests` (create 100 owners dated today, expect the 101st to be rejected with `isTooManyRequests()`) passes, and the entire existing suite remains green.",
